= Ground Transportation and Rail

== Transit Philosophy and Environmental Priorities

Ground transportation choices impact both partnership expenditure and our collective environmental footprint. Noice & Toit LLP prioritizes safe, reliable, and sustainable transit solutions. We encourage all personnel to utilize public transport networks where well-developed and safe, reserving private cars, taxis, and rideshares for situations where time constraints or logistics demand them.

== Rail Travel as the Preferred Regional Option

Modern rail transit often provides a faster, more productive journey than air travel when factoring in airport security queues and ground transfers.

#card-do("Book train travel for journeys under four hours")[
  Choose rail transit when traveling between well-connected metropolitan centers such as London to Paris, Frankfurt to Berlin, Zurich to Geneva, or New York to Washington DC. Trains offer uninterrupted productive work environments, power outlets, and downtown-to-downtown convenience.
]

#card-do("Use standard second class as the default")[
  Standard Second Class (Standard Class) is the firm standard for rail travel. First Class rail travel is permissible only when the continuous scheduled journey exceeds four (4) hours and the traveler requires a quiet working environment to prepare billable deliverables.
]

=== Rail Season Passes and Transit Cards
If your project requires daily or weekly regional rail travel, request a temporary regional travel card (such as a German BahnCard, Swiss Half-Fare card, or UK Season ticket). Finance will reimburse the pass cost if the projected ticket savings exceed the card purchase price.

== City Transit, Taxis, and Ride-Hailing

Public transit systems (subways, underground networks, trams, and airport express trains) are the preferred mode of city travel across London, Berlin, New York, Zurich, and Singapore.

#card-do("Use public transit when practical and safe")[
  Use airport express rail links (such as the Heathrow Express, Berlin FEX, or JFK AirTrain) and city subway lines for routine travel between hotels, offices, and client locations. Upload ticket stubs, contactless payment receipts, or transit card top-up statements to your expense report.
]

#card-do("Take standard taxis or ride-shares when justified")[
  Taxis and standard ride-hailing services (e.g., UberX, Lyft Standard, FreeNow) are appropriate when:
  - Traveling with bulky presentation displays, trial bundles, or heavy client equipment.
  - Arriving at an unfamiliar or remote destination late at night (after 21:00 local time).
  - Traveling between consecutive offsite meetings where public transit would cause schedule failure.
  - Multiple employees are traveling together, making a shared taxi more economical than multiple transit tickets.
]

#card-dont("Book premium or luxury rideshare categories")[
  Never order premium rideshare tiers such as Uber Black, Uber Lux, Lyft Lux, or private chauffeur services. If a standard vehicle is unavailable due to surge conditions, book a standard licensed street taxi. Premium rideshare surcharges will be deducted from your reimbursement.
]

== Rental Cars: Booking, Categories, and Insurance

Rental cars should be considered only when public transit, rail, and rideshare options are unavailable, or when visiting multiple rural client manufacturing sites in a single day.

=== Vehicle Sizing and Categories
Employees must book rental cars through our corporate portal with preferred partners (Hertz, Enterprise, National). The authorized booking class is *Compact* or *Intermediate*. Full-size vehicles, SUVs, and luxury sedans require advance written justification approved by a Practice Leader.

#card-do("Refuel the vehicle before returning it")[
  Always refuel the vehicle at a standard petrol station before returning it to the rental depot. Rental car agency refueling charges include substantial markup fees (often 200% to 300% above retail petrol prices). Keep the itemized fuel receipt to claim reimbursement.
]

#card-dont("Accept optional prepaid fuel or navigation packages")[
  Do not purchase optional prepaid fuel packages, satellite navigation system add-ons, or satellite radio subscriptions. Modern smartphones provide comprehensive navigation without extra rental fees.
]

=== Collision Damage and Rental Insurance
- *Within North America*: Decline optional Collision Damage Waiver (CDW) and Loss Damage Waiver (LDW) when renting with our corporate credit card, as comprehensive coverage is provided centrally through our firm insurance program.
- *International Rentals*: In European and Asian jurisdictions where statutory third-party liability and comprehensive insurance are not automatically covered by corporate cards, select standard mandatory CDW coverage at the rental counter.

== Personal Vehicle Usage and Mileage Reimbursement

Employees may use their personal vehicles for approved business travel when other transit forms are impractical.

#card-do("Log business mileage accurately")[
  Reimbursement for personal vehicle usage is calculated at fixed statutory rates:
  - *European Union*: €0.38 per kilometer.
  - *United States*: \$0.67 per mile (IRS conforming rate).
  - *United Kingdom*: £0.45 per mile up to 10,000 miles per tax year.
  This rate covers all fuel, oil, regular maintenance, tire wear, insurance coverage, and vehicle depreciation. To claim mileage, provide an itemized log listing the date, departure address, destination address, client matter, and verified odometer or map distance.
]

#card-dont("Claim personal commuting miles")[
  Never claim mileage or transit fares for daily travel between your home residence and your regular assigned office. Commuting is a personal living expense under statutory tax law and cannot be reimbursed or deducted by the firm.
]

== Parking Fees, Tolls, and Congestion Charges

- *Reimbursable*: Business-related toll charges (e.g., bridge tolls, highway turnpikes), municipal congestion charges (e.g., London Congestion Charge, Central Manhattan Tolling), and reasonable airport long-term parking when traveling on multi-day assignments.
- *Non-Reimbursable*: Premium valet parking fees at hotels when self-parking is available, airport short-term hourly parking for extended trips, and traffic or parking citation penalties.

== Frequently Asked Questions

*Q: Can I rent an electric vehicle (EV) even if the rental price is slightly higher?*\
A: Yes. In alignment with our sustainability initiative, renting an electric or hybrid vehicle in the compact or intermediate class is permitted and encouraged. Charging costs incurred at commercial charging stations are fully reimbursable with receipt.

*Q: What if I am involved in a traffic collision while driving a rental car on business?*\
A: First, ensure all parties are safe and notify local emergency services if necessary. Then, immediately contact the rental agency emergency line and notify Noice & Toit Legal Operations within 24 hours so our corporate insurer can open a claim file.
